    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I enjoy math mostly through its problem-solving aspect—it’s like a puzzle that reveals patterns. While I find some concepts (like abstract algebra) fascinating, others (like calculus) can be intimidating due to their complexity, especially when tackled in isolation. It thrills me how it connects to real-world phenomena, but I often prefer visualizing problems through graphs or real examples rather than purely theoretical approaches.",
